  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Child Protection and GBV Response Mavambo Transitional Phase</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mavambo Orphan Care responds to the educational, protection, legal, material, nutritional and psychosocial needs of orphaned and other vulnerable children in Mabvuku, Tafara, Caledonia and rural Goromonzi.  Mavambo&#x2019;s core strategy is offering an accelerated educational program to orphans and vulnerable illiterate children aged between 8-12 years who have never been to school.  These children are enrolled for an accelerated learning program in which they are taught basic literacy and numeracy for a period of one to two years depending on the capacity of the child. However, the period has been greatly affected by COVID-19 induced lockdowns and restrictions resulting in them taking longer to complete the MLC curriculum. Upon completion, these children graduate into formal primary school to further their education in Mabvuku and Tafara communities. After primary education they proceed into secondary education under support.</narrative>
  </description>
